## SeqSetup — the MongoDB root credential, for the mongod container only.
## Copy to `.env.db` and fill in a real password. .env.db is gitignored.
##
## This is a separate file on purpose: the app service reads the whole of
## .env, so a root credential kept there would be handed to the app as well,
## which never needs it (outside review F12). Nothing in this file reaches
## the app container.
##
## mongod creates this user itself on FIRST START ONLY. Changing the password
## here later does nothing: the value is read by MongoDB's own initdb step,
## which never runs again once the data volume exists. See
## docs/getting-started/deployment.rst, "Upgrading an existing deployment".
##
## Generate the password with `openssl rand -hex 24`, and use nothing else.
## Compose's env-file parser changes some values before mongod ever sees
## them -- measured: `$HOME` is replaced with the HOST's value, `$$` becomes
## `$`, a wrapping " or ' is stripped, and a ` #' cuts the rest of the line.
## None of it is reported. docker/mongo-init.sh itself takes any character
## (it passes the value to mongosh as an argument, not inside a URI); it is
## the env-file parser, not the script, that is the limit.

MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_USERNAME=root
MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_PASSWORD=
